      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, done in patch set 3. Closing the socket alone did not guarantee it: a read can already have completed, and Beast returns frames it already holds in its buffer without reading the socket. onUserRevoked() now sets a revoked flag before it closes the socket, and afterRead() takes the close path whenever the flag is set, even after a successful read. The new test NoMessageHandledAfterUserLosesAccess sends two messages in one read and removes the user while the first is being handled; with patch set 2 the second message was still handled.",
